# 5. Entity vs Aggregate vs Module

Do not treat every database table as an independent business entity.

Use these distinctions:

### Entity

An object with a stable identity and lifecycle.

Examples:

* Account
* Budget
* Goal
* Payee
* Reminder

### Value Object

An immutable object defined by its value.

Examples:

* Money
* Currency
* DateRange
* RecurrenceRule
* TransactionType

### Aggregate

A consistency boundary that controls changes to related data.

For example:

```text
Transaction Aggregate
    ├── Transaction
    ├── Transaction Splits
    └── Transaction Metadata
```

An aggregate must protect its invariants.

### Module

A business capability that owns related entities, use cases, and rules.

Example:

```text
Transactions Module
    ├── Expense
    ├── Income
    ├── Transfer
    ├── Refund
    └── Transaction History
```

Do not force every small concept to become a separate module if it creates unnecessary complexity.

---

# 6. Entity Ownership & Responsibility Matrix

| Module           | Owns                                                               | Must Not Own                  |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------- |
| Authentication   | Identity, sessions, access, account security                       | Transaction data              |
| Categories       | Category definitions, hierarchy, category rules                    | Actual transaction amounts    |
| Labels           | User-defined classification labels                                 | Budget calculations           |
| Accounts         | Account identity, account type, account lifecycle                  | UI dashboard summaries        |
| Budgets          | Budget definitions, limits, periods, budget rules                  | Raw account persistence       |
| Goals            | Targets, contribution rules, progress rules                        | General transaction storage   |
| Transactions     | Financial events, transaction lifecycle, classification references | Notification delivery         |
| Planned Payments | Future payment definitions, recurrence, payment lifecycle          | Direct UI reminders           |
| Payees           | People / organizations and their identity                          | Global debt calculations      |
| User Preferences | User-specific display and behavior settings                        | Financial business records    |
| Reminders        | Reminder definitions, schedules, status                            | Core transaction mutation     |
| AI Control       | AI permissions, capabilities, approval policies, audit rules       | Unrestricted financial writes |

